A compact preview tile - the small square beside a file, a list row or a media item.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/thumbnail)

<%= embed UI::ThumbnailPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Thumbnail(src: "/photos/summit.jpg", alt: "Mountain peak")

Thumbnail(variant: :icon_primary) { Icon(:bolt) }
```

One component covers two jobs:

- **Image** (`variant: :image`, the default) shows `src:` cropped to fill. Like an
  [Avatar](<%= page_path(:avatar) %>) it preloads the image and shows a placeholder icon until it
  loads, and keeps it when the image is missing or fails.
- **Icon** (`variant: :icon_*`) is a colored tile around the icon you pass as the block.

Everything is sized in `em` from `size:` - a preset (`:"2xs"` to `:"2xl"`) or a pixel number - so
the tile and its icon scale together. `shape: :circle` makes a full circle.

