## API reference

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `variant:` | `:image`, `:icon_soft`, `:icon_outline`, `:icon_primary`, `:icon_primary_outline`, `:icon_secondary`, `:icon_error`, `:icon_success`, `:icon_warning`, `:icon_info` | `:image` | An image tile or a colored icon tile. |
| `size:` | `:"2xs"`, `:xs`, `:sm`, `:md`, `:lg`, `:xl`, `:"2xl"` or pixels | `:md` | A preset, or an exact pixel size. |
| `shape:` | `:rounded`, `:circle` | `:rounded` | Rounded square or full circle. |
| `src:` | `String` | - | Image URL (image variant). |
| `alt:` | `String` | `""` | Describes the image; empty for a decorative one. |

The image loader is Avatar's `ui--avatar` controller: the tile's `data-status` moves through
`loading`, `loaded` and `error`, and `ui--avatar:loading-status-change` fires with `{ status }`.

## Accessibility

- Give a meaningful image an `alt:`; leave it empty when the thumbnail is decorative.
- Icon tiles carry no name of their own - let the surrounding text (a filename, a title) name them.
- The placeholder icon is `aria-hidden`.
